Z||000000||Scott2M4||11-02-1999||09:56 AM||||Well, it finally happened yesterday!  After weeks and weeks of searching, I finally got my first Fiero.<P>A white '87 is finally sitting in my driveway - a one-owner, never wrecked but meticulously maintained and always garaged 4 cylinder 5-speed with 110,000 miles on the dial!<P>Here's to a long and happy relationship with my first Fiero and all of you!<P>:SSH||||reg||10
Z||000001||deceler8||11-02-1999||10:12 AM||||Funny, I had been looking for mine for what seemed like months, and when I gave up looking and just assumed it would be next spring or summer before I started looking again, one showed up a few miles from me and for less money than I had figured.<P>Now all you have to work on is getting the "junior" removed from your logon. You're probably 29 posts away, which will take little time as there's so much going on here.<P>There are few cars that have this kind of following, which was one of the factors in my wanting one. The degree of knowledge present on this board is nothing short of amazing. Use it and enjoy your wheels. ||||reg||10
Z||000002||2M4 Dale||11-02-1999||10:13 AM||||Good For You SCOTT2M4, I also have my first Fiero that I bought back in March. It's an 87 coupe/black/4cly./5spd. You'll have fun in it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroshop||11-02-1999||10:48 AM||||Cogradulations on your first Fiero. My experience started when the Fiero first came out. I waas a sales manager for a pontiac dealership and we sold a ton of them. I actually did not own a Fiero until 1992 when I bought my first one and that was an 84 coupe. That was stolen a few years later and in 1996 I bought my 88 GT and since then my wife and I have a total of 10 Fieros ranging from 84 coupes to 88 GT. We also opened up a Fiero Shop because we like the car and there was a need for a shop like this one in the San Francisco Bay Area. Good luck with your new car.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ChadMan||11-02-1999||01:06 PM||||Congratulations, Scott!  A nice 4-banger can be a lot of fun - I was looking for a V6 when I came across my 88 Coupe and have never regretted buying it.  Good luck!||||reg||14
Z||000005||ggarsk||11-02-1999||01:14 PM||||Congrats Scott and welcome to the ranks. I've only had my '84 for 3 months and enjoy it a lot. I just bought another '84 for parts and I'll probally buy an '85 for parts this weekend. All 4 cylinders. I'm also looking at a '86 V6 that is in cherry condition with every option on it. They want 1500 for it but it won't go into gear. You might say I got the fever!||||reg||1
Z||000006||SCCA FIERO||11-02-1999||08:07 PM||||Welcome M8! I got my first Fiero at age 16 and have never been without one. I am sure when I am too old to get in and out of it I will still keep it to look at  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. Now if my wife would let me get a second one...||||reg||6
