Z||000014||Scott2M4||11-05-1999||05:28 AM||||To follow-up on this ... I decided to take it to my mechanic - just to have him look it over, you know, tell me what's wrong with it.  Thought I'd post the results (complete with prices) here for comments:<P>Clutch master cylinder            $ 225<BR>Valve cover resealed              $  75<BR>RF tie rod, steering damper, shocks and wheel alignment       $ 475 (est)<BR>Starter                           $ 170<BR>Serpentine belt                   $ 100<BR>---------------------------------------<BR>Total                             $1045<P>He also missed the fact that the horn and emergency brake do not work.  Sounds like I need a new mechanic.<P>Hey, Fieroshop!  What does it cost to ship a car back and forth from Ohio to San Francisco!?     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Scott2M4 (edited 11-05-1999).]||||reg||4
Z||000015||fiero56||11-05-1999||09:26 AM||||Hey, I see your from Springboro, maybe we'll see each other on the road sometime <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">. I'm just down 741 in Centerville.  <BR>Some of the prices that guy quoted you are so far inflated, there's no way he could justify them.  i.e.-master cylinder: brand new GM only costs $110 and the Fiero store only charges $97.  I don't know about the other prices, but they are probably way over also.  You might even be able to do some of the work yourself and save a few bucks.||||reg||10
Z||000016||ChadMan||11-05-1999||09:28 AM||||Oh no!  Scott, you can do most of these jobs yourself if you have common hand tools, a jack and jack stands, and a friend to help you bleed the master cylinder.  The suspension work is the only thing I might leave to a professional.<P>I have done the following jobs myself (and I'd describe myself as merely a "pretty good" shade-tree mechanic).  Here's how long it took and what it cost me:<P>New valve cover gasket - 1 hr - $7<BR>Replace starter - 1.5 hrs - $50<BR>Clutch master cylinder - 1.5 hrs - $90<P>I've never replaced a serpentine belt, but it's supposed to be way easier than replacing the old V-belt type.  E-mail me if you want tips on these jobs.<P>||||reg||11
Z||000017||Racer 1||11-05-1999||03:00 PM||||Scott2M4 all those prices are rip offs. <P>Clutch cylinder $120.00<BR>Valve cover sealed $7.00<BR>starter $90.00<BR>sepentinebelt $10.00<P>Do it yourself it not hard just acouple of hours getting scrapped knuckels!<P>I liked the serpentine one the best $100.00 I would have started to laugh out loud if that was me standing there while the garage guy said that.<P>Just make sure you get the right master cylinder....<BR> <A HREF="http://fierorob.homepage.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://fierorob.homepage.com/</A> <P>||||reg||13
